From 12e534ec20b22d34f957d35b777985bf80776ae3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: engineering <dev@atc.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 08:22:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Hero: blueprint draws in, then crossfades into a
 live-rotating 3D model

- Add js/hero-3d.js: Three.js scene that loads assests/models/atc-building.glb
  (your Tripo3D export). Falls back to a procedural placeholder building
  if the GLB isn't present yet, so the hero never looks broken mid-workflow.
- Rewrite js/hero-animation.js into a full state machine: draw blueprint
  -> hold -> crossfade to 3D -> rotate & hold -> crossfade back -> retract
  -> loop. Status badge text updates per phase.
- index.html: wrap the SVG panel and a new canvas panel in #hero-stage so
  they can crossfade in place; load three.js r128 + GLTFLoader from CDN.
- css/pages/home.css: absolute-position both panels, opacity/scale
  crossfade transition, matching grid + frame styling on the 3D panel.
